      "document_hash": "86f5d456d8897c95feb3383bfb3e6cdb0c79c0de5890488dc7f6ace536ced968",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86f5d456d889-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nD. TODD DOSS, ESQ., Lake City, Florida; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nCAROLYN M. SNURKOWSKI, ESQ., Assistant Deputy Attorney General, Tallahassee, Florida; on behalf of the Respondents.\nKANNON K. SHANMUGAM, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-05-8794",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86f5d456d8897c95feb3383bfb3e6cdb0c79c0de5890488dc7f6ace536ced968",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86f5d456d889-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In Nelson v. Campbell, this Court held that a challenge to procedures to execute an inmate may be brought in a section 1983 action unless the challenge would necessarily prevent the State from carrying out its execution."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2005-05-8794",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86f5d456d8897c95feb3383bfb3e6cdb0c79c0de5890488dc7f6ace536ced968",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86f5d456d889-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Which you decline to specify. Right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2005-05-8794",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86f5d456d8897c95feb3383bfb3e6cdb0c79c0de5890488dc7f6ace536ced968",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86f5d456d889-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Do you know of any method that has been used -- used throughout the country that is not a violation of the Eighth Amendment?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-05-8794",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86f5d456d8897c95feb3383bfb3e6cdb0c79c0de5890488dc7f6ace536ced968",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86f5d456d889-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DOSS: No, absolutely not. It's -- it's that it's -- it's that it's wanton and -- and gratuitous pain."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Doss",
      "case_id": "2005-05-8794",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86f5d456d8897c95feb3383bfb3e6cdb0c79c0de5890488dc7f6ace536ced968",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86f5d456d889-0001-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We filed other pleadings in the court that were denied regarding mental retardation, regarding a Roper claim, and various other -- other claims. Ultimately, we also filed in regards to the public records claim and us being denied the public records and the ability to assess the protocol."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2005-05-8794",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86f5d456d8897c95feb3383bfb3e6cdb0c79c0de5890488dc7f6ace536ced968",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86f5d456d889-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May -- may I ask you to clarify one thing? I take it, at this point, there"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2005-05-8794",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86f5d456d8897c95feb3383bfb3e6cdb0c79c0de5890488dc7f6ace536ced968",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86f5d456d889-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can I just clarify one thing for myself? Do I correctly understand that the Federal district court -- I'm not talking about the State court -- did not rule on the merits of your claim, but merely held that 1983 is not the proper method of pursuing the claim?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Carolyn M. Snurkowski",
      "case_id": "2005-05-8794",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86f5d456d8897c95feb3383bfb3e6cdb0c79c0de5890488dc7f6ace536ced968",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86f5d456d889-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The State is here today to suggest that the method that -- to challenge these claims is by habeas corpus, and that the Federal district court, as well as the Eleventh Circuit, was correct in finding that the district court had correctly found it had no jurisdiction because, in fact, it was a functional equivalent of the habeas corpus."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Carolyn M. Snurkowski",
      "case_id": "2005-05-8794",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86f5d456d8897c95feb3383bfb3e6cdb0c79c0de5890488dc7f6ace536ced968",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86f5d456d889-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "lethal injection is the method by which Florida is to execute individuals. The Department of Corrections, through rulemaking process internally, provides protocols for the execution day and other protocols with regard to the execution team performing its function on that given day and -- and hours leading up to that. And that has not been changed nor modified, nor has it been challenged --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-05-8794",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86f5d456d8897c95feb3383bfb3e6cdb0c79c0de5890488dc7f6ace536ced968",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86f5d456d889-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Suppose there had been a hearing and it was proved more probable than not that in some cases -- not in all, but in some cases -- use of this injection would cause excruciating pain. Would the Petitioner who is objecting being exposed to that have to come up with an alternative in order to avoid the risk of excruciating pain?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Carolyn M. Snurkowski",
      "case_id": "2005-05-8794",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86f5d456d8897c95feb3383bfb3e6cdb0c79c0de5890488dc7f6ace536ced968",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86f5d456d889-0001-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, I think the answer is twofold. First of all, the fact that the articles out there reflect that there's a potential that that could happen, there's not been evidence that it has occurred or has happened, which has been necessarily what is the precursor to when there has been changes in the method of execution because there has been a history where, in fact, a botched execution has occurred no matter what the method may have been."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE STEVENS",
      "case_id": "2005-05-8794",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86f5d456d8897c95feb3383bfb3e6cdb0c79c0de5890488dc7f6ace536ced968",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86f5d456d889-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "BUT YOUR PROCEDURE, IF I UNDERSTAND IT, WOULD BE PROHIBITED TO BE APPLIED TO DOGS OR CATS."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-05-8794",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86f5d456d8897c95feb3383bfb3e6cdb0c79c0de5890488dc7f6ace536ced968",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86f5d456d889-0002-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF KANNON K. SHANMUGAM ON BEHALF OF THE UNITED STATES, AS AMICUS CURIAE, SUPPORTING THE RESPONDENTS"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "KANNON K. SHANMUGAM (United States)",
      "case_id": "2005-05-8794",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86f5d456d8897c95feb3383bfb3e6cdb0c79c0de5890488dc7f6ace536ced968",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86f5d456d889-0002-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "METHOD OF EXECUTION BUT FAILS TO IDENTIFY A PERMISSIBLE ALTERNATIVE, THAT CLAIM IS FUNCTIONALLY EQUIVALENT TO A CLAIM CHALLENGING THE PRISONER'S DEATH SENTENCE PER SE AND THEREFORE MUST BE BROUGHT --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE SCALIA",
      "case_id": "2005-05-8794",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86f5d456d8897c95feb3383bfb3e6cdb0c79c0de5890488dc7f6ace536ced968",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86f5d456d889-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "WHY IS THAT? WHY IS THAT?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "KANNON K. SHANMUGAM (United States)",
      "case_id": "2005-05-8794",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86f5d456d8897c95feb3383bfb3e6cdb0c79c0de5890488dc7f6ace536ced968",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86f5d456d889-0002-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "AT A MINIMUM, THE ALTERNATIVE HAS TO BE ONE THAT IS PERMISSIBLE UNDER CURRENTLY GOVERNING LAW."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "D. TODD DOSS",
      "case_id": "2005-05-8794",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86f5d456d8897c95feb3383bfb3e6cdb0c79c0de5890488dc7f6ace536ced968",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86f5d456d889-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "THAT IS TRUE. THAT IS TRUE, AND WE WOULD BE PREPARED TO DO THAT IF WE WERE ALLOWED TO GO BACK AND -- AND PROCEED."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE ALITO",
      "case_id": "2005-05-8794",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86f5d456d8897c95feb3383bfb3e6cdb0c79c0de5890488dc7f6ace536ced968",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86f5d456d889-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "SUPPOSE YOU -- SUPPOSE YOU NEVER WERE TOLD BY FLORIDA WHAT THE -- HOW EXACTLY IT WAS GOING TO BE DONE."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE SCALIA",
      "case_id": "2005-05-8794",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86f5d456d8897c95feb3383bfb3e6cdb0c79c0de5890488dc7f6ace536ced968",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86f5d456d889-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "SUPPOSE -- SUPPOSE THEY DID SET IT FORTH BUT RESERVED THE RIGHT TO CHANGE IT."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE SCALIA",
      "case_id": "2005-05-8794",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "86f5d456d8897c95feb3383bfb3e6cdb0c79c0de5890488dc7f6ace536ced968",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86f5d456d889-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "NO. THIS IS THE CURRENT METHOD THAT WE INTEND TO USE IN ALL FUTURE EXECUTIONS. PERIOD. WE MAY CHANGE OUR MIND."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2005-05-8794",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "86f5d456d8897c95feb3383bfb3e6cdb0c79c0de5890488dc7f6ace536ced968",
      "evidence_id": "ev-86f5d456d889-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: No. You alleged the exact opposite in footnote 3. You said when they stonewalled you, we assumed they were going to follow Sims."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
